# agent_reporting_expert

A console agent specialized in report/presentation generation. It talks to
you about the presentation you're building, and calls tools to create,
edit, and style PowerPoint (`.pptx`) files on your behalf: slides, text,
shapes, images, native editable charts, and tables. It can also ingest
your own reference documents (`.txt`, `.md`, `.docx`, `.pdf`) so slide
content is grounded in real material instead of invented from scratch.

The LLM backend is pluggable: point it at a local model server (Ollama,
LM Studio, or anything else that speaks the OpenAI chat-completions API)
or at the hosted Anthropic Claude API.

## Project layout

```
ppt_agent/
  cli.py            Interactive console (REPL) entry point
  config.py         AgentConfig: env-var-driven settings
  llm/              Pluggable LLM connectors (base interface + backends)
  agent/            The conversation <-> tool-call loop and system prompt
  tools/            PowerPoint operations exposed to the LLM as tools
  presentation/     Stateful wrapper around the open python-pptx document
  context/          Document ingestion (txt/md/docx/pdf) + keyword search
tests/              Unit tests for the non-LLM logic
```

## Install

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
# Only if you plan to use the hosted Anthropic backend:
pip install -e ".[anthropic]"
```

## Configure

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` (or just export the variables) and adjust
for your setup. Defaults target a local Ollama server:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
export $(cat .env | xargs)   # or use your shell/direnv of choice
```

To use LM Studio instead, set `PPT_AGENT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1`
and `PPT_AGENT_MODEL` to the model loaded there. To use the hosted Claude
API, set `PPT_AGENT_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic`, `PPT_AGENT_MODEL=claude-...`,
and `PPT_AGENT_API_KEY` (or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`).

CLI flags override environment variables, e.g.:

```bash
ppt-agent --provider openai_compatible --base-url http://localhost:1234/v1 --model qwen2.5-14b-instruct
```

## Run

```bash
ppt-agent
# or: python -m ppt_agent
```

Inside the console:

```
you> /new
you> /context notes/quarterly_review.pdf
you> Create a 4-slide deck summarizing the quarterly review doc. Slide 1 title,
     slide 2 key metrics as bullets, slide 3 a bar chart of revenue by quarter,
     slide 4 next steps.
you> /save deck.pptx
```

Local (non-LLM) shortcuts: `/new`, `/open`, `/save`, `/slides`, `/context`,
`/documents`, `/reset`, `/help`, `/exit`. Anything else is sent to the
agent as a natural-language request.

## Test

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest
```
